+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-22-fix-coupon-giveback-on-cancel/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+## Context
+
+`Coupons.use(code, order)` records the order id as the single-use coupon's user. `Coupons.giveBack(code, order)` releases only if the recorded user equals `order`. `OrderService.cancel` calls `giveBack(order.coupon, order.customer)`, so the ids never match and the coupon stays used.
+
+## Decision
+
+Pass `order.id` in `cancel`. `Coupons.giveBack` already has the right semantics, including ignoring orders that did not use the coupon, so it stays as is.
+
+Free shipping at exactly €50.00 is already correct in `src/shipping.ts` (`>=`) and specified in `shipping`. We only add a regression test.
